    {
      "beat_id": "B09",
      "act": "demo — full prompt",
      "narration_text": "Feed it the whole question, 'how many r's are in strawberry,' and it comes back as eight tokens total. Strawberry isn't spelled out anywhere in there. It's just one of those eight pieces, sitting next to 'r' and apostrophe-s as equally opaque neighbors.",
      "voice": "am_puck",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "estimated_duration_s": 14,
      "shot": {
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeCodeBeat",
          "props": {
            "title": "tokenize.py — full prompt",
            "language": "python",
            "code": "enc.encode(\"How many r's are in strawberry?\")\n# 8 tokens:\n# ['How', ' many', ' r', \"'s\", ' are', ' in', ' strawberry', '?']",
            "sparkLine": "8 tokens. 'strawberry' is just one of them."
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B09.mp4",
            "at": "2026-09-28T02:08:31.434269+00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "actual_duration_s": 14.14,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B09.mp3",
      "render_duration_s": 14.166666666666666,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B09.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:ClaudeCodeBeat",
        "at": "2026-09-27T23:51:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B10",
      "act": "demo — case",
      "narration_text": "Capitalize it, and the count is still three tokens. But remember: to an AI, every token is just a numerical ID. Lowercase 'str' and capital 'Str' are assigned completely different, unrelated ID numbers. To a human, it's obviously the same word. To the model, they are just two different numbers.",
      "voice": "am_puck",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "estimated_duration_s": 13,
      "shot": {
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ExecutedData",
          "props": {
            "title": "Same word, different tokens",
            "mode": "table",
            "columnLabels": [
              "Form",
              "Tokens"
            ],
            "rows": [
              {
                "label": "'strawberry'",
                "value": 3,
                "at": 0
              },
              {
                "label": "'Strawberry'",
                "value": 3,
                "at": 0.7
              }
            ],
            "note": "same count, different IDs — str ≠ Str"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B10.mp4",
            "at": "2026-09-28T02:09:14.869187+00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "actual_duration_s": 17.73,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B10.mp3",
      "render_duration_s": 17.75,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B10.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:ExecutedData",
        "at": "2026-09-27T23:51:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B11",
      "act": "mechanism",
      "narration_text": "Here is the root of the problem. Because a token is just an ID number, it acts like a sealed box. The AI is never taught how to open that box and look at the letters inside. So when you ask 'how many r's are in strawberry', the AI has no way to actually count. It can only blindly guess based on whatever answer it saw most often during its training.",
      "voice": "am_puck",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "estimated_duration_s": 16,
      "actual_duration_s": 18.13,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B11.mp3",
      "render_duration_s": 18.166666666666668,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B11.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-09-27T23:51:12"
      },
      "shot": {
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "SLATE",
          "props": {}
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B12",
      "act": "boundary",
      "narration_text": "To be clear, this explains why the model fails at letter-counting. What this does NOT establish is whether future AI architectures will abandon tokens entirely. For now, this is the reality we build in.",
      "voice": "am_puck",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "estimated_duration_s": 10,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B12.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-09-27T23:51:12"
      },
      "shot": {
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "SLATE",
          "props": {}
        }
      },
      "actual_duration_s": 13.16,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B12.mp3",
      "render_duration_s": 13.166666666666666
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B13",
      "act": "fix",
      "narration_text": "Or skip asking the model to eyeball it at all. Hand the counting to code, word dot count 'r', and you get an exact answer instantly — for the same reason a calculator beats mental math. The model doesn't need to solve character-level problems it was never built to solve.",
      "voice": "am_puck",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "estimated_duration_s": 14,
      "shot": {
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "SLATE",
          "props": {}
        }
      },
      "actual_duration_s": 16.21,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B13.mp3",
      "render_duration_s": 16.25,
